  "prefLabel": "He-W 567.06 Non-Covered Services",
  "priorExpiration": "2003-12-29",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 567.06 Non-Covered Services. Non-covered services shall include, but not be limited to:\n\n(a) Replacement of hearing aids due to loss, misuse, or abuse, except as noted in He-W 567.05(e)(3);\n\n(b) FM systems, if the systems are for the sole purpose of recipient use in an educational setting and are coverable under He-M 1301;\n\n(c) Repair of hearing aids which are covered under a warranty;\n\n(d) Pocket talker repairs, batteries, accessories, except those listed in He-W 567.05(j) above, and optional telelinks;\n\n(e) A pocket talker if a hearing aid is already covered by medicaid;\n\n(f) A hearing aid if a pocket talker is already covered by medicaid, unless the criterion in He-W 567.05(i)(1) is met; and\n\n(g) Binaural hearing aids for recipients 21 years of age or over when the requirements set forth in He-W 567.05(c)(2) or He-W 567.07 have not been met.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading He-W 500); ss by #6157, eff 12-29-95, EXPIRED: 12-29-03\n\nNew. #9480, eff 5-23-09; amd by #10342, eff 6-1-13; ss by #12538, eff 5-25-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w500.html"
}
